          "anchorId": "pL",
          "facts": "Ss. 23 + 30 ICA · Partnership Act Ss. 4, 42, 69 · CPC O.2 R.2 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Question: <b>Is a partnership to carry on wagering contracts unlawful u/s 23?</b> &nbsp;|&nbsp; Answer: <b>No — wager is void, not illegal/forbidden/immoral/opposed to public policy; partnership valid.</b>",
          "issues": "",
          "arguments": "<div class=\"a1\"><b class=\"h\">Appellant (Parakh) — arguments</b>\n<ul><li>Dissolution finding unsupported by pleadings/evidence; S. 69 bars unregistered-firm suit; O.2 R.2 bars split claim.</li>\n<li>Partnership object = wager = <b>forbidden by law</b> (S. 30) + <b>public policy</b> + <b>immoral</b> → unlawful u/s 23 → void.</li>\n<li>Post-independence <b>welfare-State policy + Sruti/Smriti/Nibandha</b> condemn gambling — Court should evolve a <b>new head</b> of public policy.</li>\n<li>Hindu-law pious-obligation test of immoral (<i>avyavaharika</i>) debts should define S. 23 “immoral”.</li>\n<li><i>Chamarbaugwala</i>: gambling is <i>extra commercium</i> → no “business” → no partnership u/s 4.</li></ul>",
