          "anchorId": "pM",
          "facts": "S. 27 ICA · S. 57 Specific Relief Act (negative covenants) &nbsp;|&nbsp; Question: <b>Is a negative covenant barring similar employment during the contract term a restraint of trade?</b> &nbsp;|&nbsp; Answer: <b>No — during-term exclusive-service covenants are generally valid; post-term restraints are void.</b>",
          "issues": "",
          "arguments": "<div class=\"a1\"><b class=\"h\">Appellant (Golikari) — 3 contentions</b>\n<ul><li>Agreement = <b>restraint of trade → public policy → void u/s 27</b>.</li>\n<li>Validity needs <b>reasonableness in space/time + necessity</b> to protect property; Cl. 17 fails (any capacity, all business).</li>\n<li>Injunction only for <b>legitimate trade-secret protection</b>; Cl. 9 lifetime-wide; relies on <i>Ehrman v. Bartholomew</i> (10-year, “business” unlimited), <i>Mason v. Provident</i> (3-year post-term), <i>Herbert Morris</i>, <i>Attwood</i>, <i>Commercial Plastics</i>, <i>Gopal Paper Mills</i> (20-year bond).</li></ul>",
          "ratio": "No — during-term exclusive-service covenants are generally valid; post-term restraints are void.",
