          "ratio": "Marriage among Muhammadans is not a sacrament, but purely a civil contract. Dower is not the price of the wife, but an exchange or consideration for matrimonial consortium. Where dower is prompt, the wife can refuse consortium until payment; but once consummation has occurred with consent, non-payment of prompt dower does not bar restitution, though the decree must be made conditional upon payment of dower."
