          "question": "Rani 19 married to widower Shekhar 50 by father fraudulently telling 25 + wealthy. Veiled, shocked at wedding. Remedy?",
          "modelAnswer": "<b>ISSUE:</b> Fraud via father-agent + veil → 12(1)(c)?<br>\n<b>RULE + APPLICATION:</b> Squarely <i>Babui Panmato</i>: father’s false 25–30/affluent talk to mother-agent = suggestion false + active concealment + duty to disclose (Contract 17 + Ill.(b)); 30-yr gap material; veil prevented discovery/withdrawal; pre-marriage fraud suffices (no “at time of marriage” in (c); Anath Nath De rejected). File within 1 yr of discovery (wedding-night/15-4-60 analogy) + no post-discovery cohabitation → <b>annulment granted</b>. Add <i>Som Dutt</i> (7-yr gap + hysteria = gross fraud) + <i>Asha</i> (duty). If consummated post-discovery with consent → bar. No 494. Alimony per Sec 25."
