          "examStrategy": "(1) Grief and sorrow are NOT actionable; there must be a medically recognized psychiatric illness. (2) For secondary victims, test Alcock's 3-fold proximity: (i) close ties of love and affection, (ii) proximity in time and space (or immediate aftermath), (iii) perception through own unaided senses (television broadcast does NOT suffice).",
