          "anchorId": "c7",
          "facts": "Bird was a promoter (and director) of the Lydney and Wigpool Iron Ore Co.; he participated in the sale of property/mining rights to the company at a price above what the sellers had paid, and claimed to be entitled to keep the whole margin. The company's suit challenged the profit; the question was what the promoter could lawfully retain.",
