          "anchorId": "c8",
          "facts": "Baines and another promoted the Omnium Electric Palaces Ltd. and, at the formation, sold to it (or procured the sale of) property — machinery/land for an electric-theatre business — at a figure which included a profit for themselves. The company, later in liquidation or suit by shareholders, sought to recover the profit, arguing that the promoters were trustees and could not profit at all.",
          "issues": "Core legal question examined by the bench.",
