          "unit": "Topic 2: Promotion & Formation of a Company",
          "file": "sem 3/company/DU_Company_Law_Promotion_Formation_Notes.html",
          "anchorId": "c9",
          "facts": "Promoters sold a theatre/variety-hall property to a company they had formed at a price yielding them a large profit; the purchase was sanctioned by the shareholders without the material facts; the company went into liquidation. By the time of the liquidator's claim the property had been enjoyed and disposed of — the parties could not be restored to their original positions, so the contract could not be rescinded.",
          "issues": "Core legal question examined by the bench.",
