          "facts": "Newborne contracted for the sale of goods, signing \"for and on behalf of Sensolid (Great Britain) Ltd.\" — a company which in fact never was incorporated . The goods were delivered; the price was not paid; the seller sued the signatory personally (the company of course could not be sued).",
