          "name": "Natal Land & Colonisation Co. v. Pauline Colliery Syndicate (1904) AC 120 (PC)",
          "citation": "(1904) AC 120 (PC)",
          "unitNumber": 2,
          "unit": "Topic 2: Promotion & Formation of a Company",
          "file": "sem 3/company/DU_Company_Law_Promotion_Formation_Notes.html",
          "anchorId": "c12",
          "facts": "N. Co. entered into an agreement with one C. , who acted on behalf of a proposed syndicate , under which N. Co. was to give the syndicate a lease of coal-mining rights . The syndicate was then registered as a company , struck a seam of coal, and claimed the lease. N. Co. refused. The company sued for specific performance of the agreement, or in the alternative damages .",
          "issues": "Core legal question examined by the bench.",
