          "anchorId": "pyq-u4-3",
          "question": "H2. B Ltd, a listed NBFC, files a shelf prospectus in April 2025 (validity one year) and makes a first issue. In November it creates a new floating charge and its NPAs jump. It opens a second tranche in December without telling anyone. X applied in October with advance money. Advise X and SEBI.",
          "modelAnswer": "s. 31(2) required an information memorandum of the new charge and the change in financial position, filed with the RoC before the second offer. X, having applied before the change, had a right to be informed and to withdraw within 15 days with refund. The IM + shelf prospectus together are a prospectus (s. 31(3)), so ss. 34–37 apply to the omission. SEBI may act under s. 24 / SEBI Act ss. 11, 11B. Officers risk s. 447 if the omission was dishonest."
