          "anchorId": "pyq-u6-8",
          "question": "Distinguish ordinary and special resolutions; also show of hands, poll and postal ballot.” DU-pattern — comparison format",
          "modelAnswer": "\n\n> 🎯 **Marking Scheme & Issues:** Marks split: № 3 resolutions table (test, uses, filing, amendment-lock, special notice) · № 3 voting channels · № 2 unifying close + authorities.\n\n**Resolutions (S.114):** an **ordinary resolution** requires votes-for > votes-against (of votes cast); powers the four AGM ordinary items, director-removal (with special notice), routine approvals; no filing generally required. A **special resolution** requires (a) the intention stated as SR in the notice, and (b) votes-for ≥ **3×** votes-against; it drives constitutional change — articles (S.14), inter-state registered-office shift (S.12), capital reduction (S.66), S.180 disposals/borrowings, non-pre-emptive issues (S.62), voluntary winding-up (S.304) — and **must be filed with the RoC within 30 days (S.117)** and embodied in subsequent copies of the articles. Both are frozen by the notice: amendments changing substance void them (would a member who stayed away reasonably wish he hadn't?). A third hybrid — **OR by special notice** (S.115) — guards destabilising moves (removal of directors/auditors): 1%-holders' notice 14 days ahead, company's circulation 7 days ahead.\n\n  \n\n**Voting channels:** *show of hands* (S.107) is head-count — one member, one vote, chairman's declaration conclusive bar poll (*Dhakeswari*: unless wrongly computed); *poll* (S.109) is share-weighted — demanded by 1/10 voting power or ₹5-lakh holders, chairman-bound if demanded, adjournment/chair-polls forthwith, others within 48h, result = decision of meeting, declaration prima facie final (*Mahaliram*); *e-voting* (S.108) enfranchises scale in listed/large companies; *postal ballot* (S.110) — voting by post/electronics for statutorily reserved items and optional items — skips assembly itself (with scrutiniser and results process). **Close:** the channels form one system: hands for speed, poll for precision, e-vote/postal for reach — proxies ride all except show of hands (unless articles allow)."
